>> title: Bánh Mì Thịt Nướng
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: pork, vietnamese, sandwich, lemongrass, grill
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: banh mi thit nuong, bánh mì thịt nướng, thit nuong, thịt nướng, grilled pork banh mi, BBQ pork sandwich, lemongrass pork sandwich, grilled pork sandwich, number 2, S2
>> pairs-with: banh-mi-khong, do-chua, nuoc-cham
>> servings: 4
>> time: 4 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the marinade is lemongrass and sugar: it lacquers on the grill and then it burns, and the eight minutes is standing right there

>> step: pound to a wet paste
Pound @lemongrass{4%stalks}(tender lower third only, sliced thin) with @garlic{4%cloves} and @shallot{1} to a wet paste in a #mortar{}.

>> step: stir the marinade
Stir @&(~1)lemongrass paste{} together with @granulated sugar{3%Tbs}(38 g), @fish sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @oyster sauce{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @black pepper{1%tsp}(coarsely ground) and @vegetable oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL).

>> step: marinate chilled 4 hr
Marinate @sliced pork shoulder{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; cut across the grain in 1/4-inch slices) in @&(~1)marinade{} in the #fridge{} ~marinate{4%hr}, or overnight.

>> step: grill 8 min, until the edges lacquer
Grill @&(~1)pork{} over hot coals ~grill{8%min}, turning once, until the edges char and the sugar goes glassy.

>> step: pack the roll, dress and close
Pack @&(~1)grilled pork{} into @bánh mì rolls{4}(crisped and hinged) spread with @mayonnaise{1/4%cup}(60 mL), and fill out with @đồ chua{1%cup}(drained), @cucumber{1/2}(in batons), @cilantro{1%cup} and @bird chiles{2}(sliced).
